course: dictionary
lesson: 14199
title: A word for a climber
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mountaineer is a person who climbs mountains, often as a sport or hobby. Look for clues: mountain is the first part of the word, and the ending -eer often means a person who does something, like engineer or volunteer. «The mountaineer tied herself to a rope before she started to climb.» The rope tells you the climbing is careful and serious.
explain: Mountaineering is the sport itself, not the person. «Mountaineering needs strong legs, a good map and a lot of care.» Ask yourself: is the sentence about a person, or about the sport? If it is about the sport, the word is mountaineering.
explain: Clues around the word help you work out its meaning. «Edmund Hillary was a famous mountaineer who climbed Mount Everest.» Famous and climbed Mount Everest tell you a mountaineer climbs very high mountains. Swap in your meaning: "Edmund Hillary was a famous person who climbs mountains" still makes sense, so you are right.
fact: A mountaineer is a person who climbs mountains as a sport or hobby.
fact: Mountaineering is the sport of climbing mountains.
fact: Mountaineers often use ropes, helmets and maps to stay safe.
fact: «Edmund Hillary» and «Tenzing Norgay» were the first mountaineers known to reach the top of Mount Everest, in 1953.
fact: The ending -eer often means a person who does something, so a mountaineer is a person who does mountaineering.
exercise: «The mountaineer tied herself to a rope before she started to climb.» Who is a mountaineer? | A person who drives trains up steep hills | A person who climbs mountains as a sport or hobby | A person who draws maps of rivers | *A person who climbs mountains as a sport or hobby, using ropes and helmets
exercise: «Mountaineering needs strong legs, a good map and a lot of care.» Does this sentence name a person or a sport? | A person | *A sport | A place | A type of rope
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the sport in this sentence: «Mountaineering is hard work, but many people love it.» | people | hard | work | *Mountaineering
test: «Edmund Hillary was a famous mountaineer who climbed Mount Everest.» What does mountaineer mean? | A person who cooks on a boat | *A person who climbs mountains as a sport or hobby | A kind of tall tree | A person who climbs mountains
test: Mia says, «Mountaineers always carry a map.» What does the word tell you about a mountaineer? | They only walk on flat roads | They are good at swimming | *They climb mountains and stay safe on the way | They never leave their homes
exam: Which word means the sport of climbing mountains? | mountain | climber | mountaineer | *mountaineering
